{"title": "High ground rules", "pageid": 2185, "url": "https://bg3.wiki/wiki/High_ground_rules", "categories": ["Gameplay mechanics"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>High ground</b> is an important mechanic in Baldur's Gate 3 combat. Holding high ground over enemies grants a number of benefits including increased range and attack roll bonuses.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Attack_roll_modifiers\">Attack roll modifiers</span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:High_Ground_modifier_preview.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/9/90/High_Ground_modifier_preview.png/300px-High_Ground_modifier_preview.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/9/90/High_Ground_modifier_preview.png/450px-High_Ground_modifier_preview.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/9/90/High_Ground_modifier_preview.png 2x\"><img src=\"/w/images/thumb/9/90/High_Ground_modifier_preview.png/300px-High_Ground_modifier_preview.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"104\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/9/90/High_Ground_modifier_preview.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a><figcaption> Targeting an enemy with an attack that will receive the +2 High Ground bonus to the attack roll. </figcaption></figure>\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Low_Ground_modifier_preview.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/8/82/Low_Ground_modifier_preview.png/300px-Low_Ground_modifier_preview.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/8/82/Low_Ground_modifier_preview.png/450px-Low_Ground_modifier_preview.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/8/82/Low_Ground_modifier_preview.png 2x\"><img src=\"/w/images/thumb/8/82/Low_Ground_modifier_preview.png/300px-Low_Ground_modifier_preview.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"104\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/8/82/Low_Ground_modifier_preview.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a><figcaption> Targeting an enemy with an attack that will receive the -2 Low Ground penalty to the attack roll. </figcaption></figure>\n<p>If there is sufficient elevation difference between an attacker and target, an elevation modifier is applied to the attack roll.\nAt 2.5 m (8 ft) above a target, an attacker receives a +2 \"High Ground\" bonus to attack rolls.\nAt 2.5 m (8 ft) below a target, an attacker receives a -2 \"Low Ground\" penalty to attack rolls.\nWhen targeting an enemy, this modifier is displayed below its hit points bar with other modifiers.\n</p><p>The <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Sharpshooter\" title=\"Sharpshooter\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/9/9c/Sharpshooter_All_In_Icon.webp/20px-Sharpshooter_All_In_Icon.webp, /w/images/thumb/9/9c/Sharpshooter_All_In_Icon.webp/30px-Sharpshooter_All_In_Icon.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/9/9c/Sharpshooter_All_In_Icon.webp/40px-Sharpshooter_All_In_Icon.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Sharpshooter\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/9/9c/Sharpshooter_All_In_Icon.webp/20px-Sharpshooter_All_In_Icon.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/9/9c/Sharpshooter_All_In_Icon.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Sharpshooter\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Sharpshooter\">Sharpshooter</a> feat removes the low ground penalty for ranged weapon attack rolls.\n</p><p>These high ground rules apply to <em>all</em> attack rolls, even melee ones. However, since melee attacks seldom have a long enough range for elevation to matter, it rarely applies to them. There are a few exceptions, such as <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Thorn_Whip\" title=\"Thorn Whip\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/e/e8/Thorn_Whip_Icon.webp/20px-Thorn_Whip_Icon.webp, /w/images/thumb/e/e8/Thorn_Whip_Icon.webp/30px-Thorn_Whip_Icon.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/e/e8/Thorn_Whip_Icon.webp/40px-Thorn_Whip_Icon.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Thorn Whip\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/e/e8/Thorn_Whip_Icon.webp/20px-Thorn_Whip_Icon.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/e/e8/Thorn_Whip_Icon.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Thorn_Whip\" title=\"Thorn Whip\">Thorn Whip</a> (a melee spell attack with a range of 9 m (30 ft)), <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Fangs_of_the_Fire_Snake\" title=\"Fangs of the Fire Snake\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/d/d1/Fangs_of_the_Fire_Snake_Icon.webp/20px-Fangs_of_the_Fire_Snake_Icon.webp, /w/images/thumb/d/d1/Fangs_of_the_Fire_Snake_Icon.webp/30px-Fangs_of_the_Fire_Snake_Icon.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/d/d1/Fangs_of_the_Fire_Snake_Icon.webp/40px-Fangs_of_the_Fire_Snake_Icon.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Fangs of the Fire Snake\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/d/d1/Fangs_of_the_Fire_Snake_Icon.webp/20px-Fangs_of_the_Fire_Snake_Icon.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/d/d1/Fangs_of_the_Fire_Snake_Icon.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Fangs_of_the_Fire_Snake\" title=\"Fangs of the Fire Snake\">Fangs of the Fire Snake</a> (a melee unarmed attack with a range of 6 m (20 ft)), <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Diving_Strike\" title=\"Diving Strike\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/2/2b/Diving_Strike_Icon.webp/20px-Diving_Strike_Icon.webp, /w/images/thumb/2/2b/Diving_Strike_Icon.webp/30px-Diving_Strike_Icon.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/2/2b/Diving_Strike_Icon.webp/40px-Diving_Strike_Icon.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Diving Strike\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/2/2b/Diving_Strike_Icon.webp/20px-Diving_Strike_Icon.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/2/2b/Diving_Strike_Icon.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Diving_Strike\" title=\"Diving Strike\">Diving Strike</a> (which requires jumping from a higher elevation anyway), or <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Charger:_Weapon_Attack\" title=\"Charger: Weapon Attack\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/f/f1/Charger_Weapon_Attack_Icon.webp/20px-Charger_Weapon_Attack_Icon.webp, /w/images/thumb/f/f1/Charger_Weapon_Attack_Icon.webp/30px-Charger_Weapon_Attack_Icon.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/f/f1/Charger_Weapon_Attack_Icon.webp/40px-Charger_Weapon_Attack_Icon.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Charger\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/f/f1/Charger_Weapon_Attack_Icon.webp/20px-Charger_Weapon_Attack_Icon.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/f/f1/Charger_Weapon_Attack_Icon.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Charger:_Weapon_Attack\" title=\"Charger: Weapon Attack\">Charger</a> (when charging up or down a slope with a large enough elevation change). On the other hand, attacks with <a href=\"/wiki/Extra_Reach\" title=\"Extra Reach\">Extra Reach</a> weapons <em>do not</em> have extended vertical reach, so they do not have sufficient vertical range for high ground modifiers to apply.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Range_extension\">Range extension</span></h2>\n<p>Normally for range considerations, only the horizontal distance between an attacker and target matters and vertical distance is ignored. Specifically, the targetable region of an ability is a vertical cylinder<sup id=\"cite_ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>note 1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> (where the attacker is at the centre of this cylinder) with a radius equal to the ability's range, and not a sphere.\n</p>\nMost ranged <i>abilities</i><sup id=\"cite_ref-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>note 2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> gain increased range when targeting enemies at a lower elevation equal to the elevation difference. For example, a ranged weapon attack (range of 18 m (60 ft)) against a target 9 m (30 ft) below has a maximum horizontal range of 27 m (90 ft). In this case, the true distance between the attacker and target is <style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r330229\">@media screen and (max-width:779px){.mw-parser-output .math{text-align:center;overflow:scroll;margin:auto}}@media screen and (min-width:780px){.mw-parser-output .math{text-align:center;font-size:110%;margin:auto}}</style><div class=\"math\"><math class=\"mwe-math-element\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mtext>Distance</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">=</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><msqrt><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>7</mn><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mtext>m</mtext></mrow><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>9</mn><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mtext>m</mtext></mrow><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">=</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">.</mo><mn>4</mn><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mstyle></mrow></math></div> which is well beyond the normal range of the attack. However, there is no corresponding range penalty when attacking a target at a higher elevation.\n<p>A ranged weapon's <i>maximum effective range</i> is its <i>normal attack range</i>. Beyond this, the attacker suffers a \"Target outside normal range\" penalty which applies <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Disadvantage\" title=\"Disadvantage\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/b/b9/Disadvantage_Icon.png/27px-Disadvantage_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/b/b9/Disadvantage_Icon.png/41px-Disadvantage_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/b/b9/Disadvantage_Icon.png/55px-Disadvantage_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Disadvantage\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/b/b9/Disadvantage_Icon.png/27px-Disadvantage_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/b/b9/Disadvantage_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Disadvantage\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> to the attack roll. Unlike attack range abilities, this effective range is <i>not</i> extended by the high ground range extension. It is also measured using the true distance between the attacker and target, not just the horizontal component. Thus, maximum attack range and effective weapon range are equal at level elevations, but diverge when dealing with elevation <i>differences</i>. Practically speaking, this means this penalty is only encountered when extending the attack range with elevation, particularly high ground range extension. Spell attacks do not have a maximum effective range and do not suffer this penalty when attacking beyond normal range.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Footnotes\">Footnotes</span></h2>\n<div class=\"notebegin\">\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-1\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">For most ranged abilities, the height of this cylinder is infinite (either <code>TargetFloor</code> and <code>TargetCeiling</code> values are <code>-1</code>, or it has the <code><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=RangeIgnoreVerticalThreshold_(spell_flag)&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"RangeIgnoreVerticalThreshold (spell flag) (page does not exist)\">RangeIgnoreVerticalThreshold</a></code> spell flag). For melee ranged abilities, the height of this cylinder usually does not extend above the height of the character (<code>TargetCeiling</code> value of <code>0</code>).</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-2\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">These are all abilities with the <code><a href=\"/wiki/HasHighGroundRangeExtension_(spell_flag)\" title=\"HasHighGroundRangeExtension (spell flag)\">HasHighGroundRangeExtension</a></code> spell flag.</span>\n</li>\n</ol></div>\n</div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260714200202\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.043 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.044 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1556/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 9450/4194304 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 2409/4194304 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 17/200\nExpensive parser function count: 0/750\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2407/5000000 bytes\nExtLoops count: 0/1000\nLua time usage: 0.013/7.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 923981/52428800 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   32.405      1 -total\n 56.39%   18.274      5 Template:SmSAI\n 35.54%   11.518      6 Template:Icon_link\n 33.48%   10.850      6 Template:Icon_text\n 25.23%    8.177     12 Template:Trim\n 17.45%    5.656      1 Template:Math_block\n 10.36%    3.356      6 Template:Ifempty\n  9.46%    3.065      2 Template:Note\n  8.60%    2.786      6 Template:Icon\n  5.40%    1.751      1 Template:Disadvantage\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key bg3wiki:pcache:idhash:2185-0!canonical and timestamp 20260714200202 and revision id 323757. Rendering was triggered because: unknown\n -->\n</div>"}